{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up for #15 (PR #29). The branch was rebased onto origin/main; your commit is now 11f3314 — run `git log -1` first and work on top of it. Do not delegate further.\n\nApply each item ONLY if it removes net lines without changing behaviour; if one would add lines, skip it and say so:\n1. `src/backends/cursor/doctor.rs` has a `status_line` duplicating the one in `src/cli_info.rs`: keep one `pub(crate)` copy and use it in both.\n2. The probe-failure stderr formatting repeated in doctor.rs (the `unwrap_or_else` blocks around --version, about, --list-models): one helper `fn command_err(r: &AgentCommandResult, what: &str) -> String` (match the real type name).\n3. `src/backends/cursor/mod.rs`: merge `absorb` and `handle_line` into one function.\n4. The fixture test's `last_result` serde re-parse: replace with assertions on `parse_stdout`'s result only.\n5. Add a `// ponytail:` comment where the bad-model error is built: the exit code is not carried (clean_exit is a bool); upgrade path: carry `Option<i32>` if a backend's error text ever depends on it.\n\nThen `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` must pass. New commit (no amend), message ending `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`. Do not push.\n\nReport: commit SHA, which items applied/skipped with net line delta (`git diff --stat HEAD~1`), test summary. Then **Friction** (up to 3 bullets). STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"1d546125-183e-46a3-aaab-e9734f91ce3e"}
